{
  "task": "M1-129",
  "tree": "build/relwithdebinfo",
  "note": "The snapshot a pass restores the build tree from (register decisions 506 and 512-519). Each mutant takes away one part of the put-back -- the outputs, what the tests wrote, the second listing, the source's time, the check of git's bytes, the build's check, the second restore after it -- or one of the rules around it: a leftover snapshot, --restore, and the main loop putting the tree back after each mutant. All are judged by mutate.py's self-test, which runs the put-back on a tree of plain files and on a scratch project CMake configures and Ninja builds, and a whole two-mutant pass shaped as m1-95.json is. Two survive, declared: the order of the put-back's steps, and the check of the snapshot's copies. Since item 7 (register decisions 520-524) also Ninja's stored answers and their key, the fingerprints check's fresh reading, a judge the tree does not have -- run by ctest, at the start of a pass, in --verify and in the due-list -- a file with no mutants, and a mutant file's own mutants as its input: judged by mutants-due.py's self-test, mutate.py's, and the CTest test mutants_due_mutant_file. Since item 9's step B (register decisions 573-577): tests/TestCase.hpp's fixed line, its registration's line, its tags and the file it reports, each judged by test_test_case, each of whose cases kills one; and check-test-cases.py's rules -- a repeated section name, a section outside a test case, a computed name, a TEST_CASE without the header, a suite including Catch2's macros, and its reading of a comment -- judged by its self-test. Since the task's finish (register decisions 601-606): item 1's reproducible builds -- the clang settings taken out, judged by reproducible_build, and its script's two refusals, by that script's self-test -- and items 2-5: what the driver skips; what a fingerprint is made of, part by part, each judged by a self-test case that changes that part's input (decision 602); the read records the driver reads and the tests write, a read before the first test case among them (decision 604); and the full run and the push (decisions 484, 503, 535, 542 and 603). Judged by run_tests_self_test, run_tests_end_to_end, run_tests_in_tree, read_record_written, test_read_records, parallel_tests and the self-tests of parallel_tests and test_reads. The pre-push hook itself is mutated too: --verify accepts a mutant of a git hook that builds nothing, since git reads it as it stands, as Python reads a script (decision 613).",
